## Problem
UUID.randomUUID() at line 138 for newBubbleId breaks reproducibility.

## Pattern
```java
private volatile Supplier<UUID> uuidSupplier = UUID::randomUUID;
public void setUuidSupplier(Supplier<UUID> supplier) {
    this.uuidSupplier = supplier;
}
// Line 138: UUID newBubbleId = uuidSupplier.get();
```

## New Utility Class
```java
public class SeededUuidSupplier implements Supplier<UUID> {
    private final Random random;
    public SeededUuidSupplier(long seed) { this.random = new Random(seed); }
    public UUID get() { return new UUID(random.nextLong(), random.nextLong()); }
}
```

## TDD Requirements
1. Same seed = same bubble IDs across runs
2. Different seeds = different IDs
3. Default uses UUID.randomUUID()

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Supplier<UUID> field added
- [ ] setUuidSupplier() method
- [ ] SeededUuidSupplier class created
- [ ] Tests verify reproducibility

Branch: feature/8putk-esvt-far-pointers
Depends on: Luciferase-8putk.1 (tests must exist before implementation)

SCOPE
Three coordinated changes, all in one commit so the test suite goes green atomically:
  A. esvt_ray_traversal.cl — kernel fix (2 defects + struct comment)
  B. ESVTOpenCLRenderer.java — renderer wiring
  C. Remove @Disabled from kernelSource_containsFarPointersArg if it was added in .1

DO NOT TOUCH: traverseESVTBeam — it is a non-traversing stub (no getChildIndex call).

--- CHANGE A: render/src/main/resources/kernels/esvt_ray_traversal.cl ---

1. Fix getChildPtr mask (:179-181). Current: `& 0x3FFFu` (14 bits). Change to `& 0x7FFFu` (15 bits).
   Precedent: ESVTNodeUnified.CHILD_PTR_MASK=0xFFFE0000 covers bits 17-31 = 15 bits.

2. Fix getChildIndex far-branch (:187-197). Current:
     if (isFar(node)) {
         childPtr = nodes[parentIdx + childPtr].childDescriptor;
     }
   Replace with:
     if (isFar(node)) {
         childPtr = (uint) farPointers[childPtr];
     }
   This matches CPU: ESVTData.resolveChildPtr / ESVTNodeUnified.getChildIndex uses
   farPointers[index] as a RELATIVE offset; result = parentIdx + childPtr + offset (line 196 unchanged).

3. Add farPointers parameter to getChildIndex signature (:187):
   Change: uint getChildIndex(__global const ESVTNode* nodes, ESVTNode node, int childIdx, uint parentIdx)
   To:     uint getChildIndex(__global const ESVTNode* nodes, __global const int* farPointers, ESVTNode node, int childIdx, uint parentIdx)
   Update all call sites of getChildIndex inside the kernel to pass farPointers.

4. Add farPointers to traverseESVT kernel signature (:620-626). Current args:
     rays, nodes, contours, hitResults, hitNormals, maxDepth
   New args (insert after nodes, renumber all setRawBufferArg calls to match B below):
     rays(0), nodes(1), farPointers(2), contours(3), hitResults(4), hitNormals(5), maxDepth(6)
   Pass farPointers through to all getChildIndex call sites within traverseESVT.

5. Fix stale struct comment "childptr(14)" — update to "childptr(15)".
   Update layout comment to: [childptr(15)|far(1)|childmask(8)|leafmask(8)]

--- CHANGE B: render/src/main/java/com/hellblazer/luciferase/esvt/gpu/ESVTOpenCLRenderer.java ---

1. Add field (mirror ESVOOpenCLRenderer line 63):
     private long clFarPointerBuffer;

2. allocateTypeSpecificBuffers: initialize clFarPointerBuffer = 0 (alongside clNodeBuffer).

3. uploadDataBuffers (currently :154-180):
   After uploading the contour buffer, add far-pointer upload block mirroring
   ESVOOpenCLRenderer.uploadDataBuffers (:115-150):
     if (clFarPointerBuffer != 0) {
         clReleaseMemObject(clFarPointerBuffer);
         untrackRawHandle(clFarPointerBuffer);
         clFarPointerBuffer = 0;
     }
     var farPointers = data.farPointers();   // int[] from ESVTData
     if (farPointers != null && farPointers.length > 0) {
         var fpData = memAlloc(farPointers.length * Integer.BYTES);
         fpData.order(ByteOrder.nativeOrder());
         for (int fp : farPointers) { fpData.putInt(fp); }
         fpData.flip();
         try {
             clFarPointerBuffer = createRawBuffer(fpData, CL_MEM_READ_ONLY | CL_MEM_COPY_HOST_PTR);
         } finally {
             memFree(fpData);
