- Defensive against contract violations?

**Options**:

**Option A: Remove entirely** (RECOMMENDED):
```java
CompletableFuture.allOf(futures.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0])).join();
// Update states immediately - components use volatile/atomic per contract
for (var comp : componentsToStop) {
    states.put(comp.name(), comp.getState());
}
```

**Option B: Keep with clear justification**:
```java
CompletableFuture.allOf(futures.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0])).join();
// Sleep to allow OS thread scheduling to complete before reading states
// Required on platforms with weak memory ordering (e.g., ARM)
// TODO: Replace with explicit memory barrier if available
try {
