## Implementation Plan

**Goal**: Document memory visibility requirements for component state storage.

**Problem**: Coordinator assumes component state changes are visible across threads. Component using plain (non-volatile) field can cause stale reads:

```java
class BadComponent implements LifecycleComponent {
    private LifecycleState state;  // NOT volatile - BAD!

    public CompletableFuture<Void> start() {
        state = RUNNING;  // No memory barrier - invisible to other threads
        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(null);
    }

    public LifecycleState getState() {
        return state;  // Stale read from coordinator's thread
    }
}
```

**Impact**: Coordinator makes wrong lifecycle decisions based on stale state.

**Solution**: Document in LifecycleComponent interface:

```java
/**
 * Lifecycle component interface for coordinator management.
 * 
 * <p><b>Memory Visibility Requirement</b>: Implementations MUST use volatile
 * fields or java.util.concurrent.atomic classes for state storage to ensure
 * proper cross-thread visibility. State changes MUST be visible to other
 * threads without additional synchronization.
 * 
 * <p><b>Recommended Pattern</b>:
 * <pre>
 * private final AtomicReference&lt;LifecycleState&gt; state = 
 *     new AtomicReference&lt;&gt;(LifecycleState.CREATED);
 * 
 * public LifecycleState getState() {
 *     return state.get();
 * }
 * </pre>
 * 
 * @author hal.hildebrand
 */
public interface LifecycleComponent {
    // ... methods
}
```

