Implement performance optimizations for WebSocket streaming.

## Optimizations
1. **Batch region sending** - reduce WebSocket send() overhead
2. **ByteBuffer pooling** - reduce GC pressure from binary frame encoding
3. **Endpoint cache helper** - extract repetitive pattern

### 1. Batch Region Sending
**Location**: RegionStreamer.java:429-467

```java
private void streamToClient(ClientSession session) {
    var diff = viewportTracker.diffViewport(session.sessionId);
    if (diff.isEmpty()) return;

    var framesToSend = new ArrayList<ByteBuffer>();

    for (var visibleRegion : diff.added()) {
        if (session.pendingSends.get() >= config.maxPendingSendsPerClient()) {
            break;
        }

        if (regionCache != null) {
            var cached = regionCache.get(new RegionCache.CacheKey(...));
            cached.ifPresent(cr -> framesToSend.add(BinaryFrameCodec.encode(cr.builtRegion())));
        }
    }

    if (!framesToSend.isEmpty()) {
        sendBinaryFramesBatch(session, framesToSend);
    }
}
```

### 2. ByteBuffer Pooling
**Location**: RegionStreamer.java:486-491

```java
private static final ThreadLocal<ByteBuffer> BUFFER_POOL = 
    ThreadLocal.withInitial(() -> ByteBuffer.allocateDirect(1024 * 1024));

private void sendBinaryFrameAsync(ClientSession session, RegionCache.CachedRegion cachedRegion) {
    var buffer = BUFFER_POOL.get();
    buffer.clear();
    var frame = BinaryFrameCodec.encode(builtRegion, buffer);
    // ...
}
```

### 3. Cache Helper Extraction
**Location**: RenderingServer.java:444-449, 526-531

```java
private <T> void handleWithCache(Context ctx, String cacheKey, Supplier<T> compute) {
    String cached = endpointCache.getIfPresent(cacheKey);
    if (cached != null) {
        ctx.contentType("application/json").result(cached);
        return;
    }

    T response = compute.get();
    try {
        String jsonString = JSON_MAPPER.writeValueAsString(response);
        endpointCache.put(cacheKey, jsonString);
        ctx.contentType("application/json").result(jsonString);
    } catch (Exception e) {
        log.error("Failed to serialize response", e);
        ctx.json(response);
    }
}
```

## Testing
