When X-axis split causes collision, try alternative split planes to allow continued splitting.

## Problem
Current split always uses X-axis normal: `new SplitPlane(new Point3f(1.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f), worldCentroid.x)`

When a bubble at L1 splits, child goes to L2. If same bubble tries to split again:
- Same centroid → same split plane → same child key → collision
- Bubble stuck at NEEDS_SPLIT but can't actually split

## Solution Options

### Option A: Rotate through axes
\`\`\`java
// Track which axis was used for each bubble's last split
Map<UUID, Integer> lastSplitAxis = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

int axis = (lastSplitAxis.getOrDefault(bubbleId, -1) + 1) % 3;
Point3f normal = switch(axis) {
    case 0 -> new Point3f(1, 0, 0); // X
    case 1 -> new Point3f(0, 1, 0); // Y
    case 2 -> new Point3f(0, 0, 1); // Z
};
float distance = switch(axis) {
    case 0 -> worldCentroid.x;
    case 1 -> worldCentroid.y;
    case 2 -> worldCentroid.z;
};
lastSplitAxis.put(bubbleId, axis);
\`\`\`

### Option B: Entity clustering analysis
\`\`\`java
// Use ClusteringDetector to find natural partition
var clusters = clusteringDetector.detectClusters(bubble, 2);
var splitPlane = clusteringDetector.computeSplitPlane(clusters);
\`\`\`

### Option C: Retry with different axis on collision
\`\`\`java
for (int axis = 0; axis < 3; axis++) {
    var splitPlane = createSplitPlane(worldCentroid, axis);
    var result = executor.execute(new SplitProposal(..., splitPlane, ...));
    if (result.success()) break;
    // Try next axis
}
\`\`\`

