## Implementation Plan

**Current Test 29** (lines 947-995):
100 iterations of concurrent registerAndStart + unregister, but no cleanup between iterations.

**Issue**: Successfully registered components accumulate, may affect later iterations.

**Solution**: Add cleanup in finally block:

```java
for (int i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {
    var component = new MockComponent("test-" + i);

    try {
        // Thread A: registerAndStart
        var registerFuture = executor.submit(() -> {
            try {
                coordinator.registerAndStart(component);
            } catch (Exception e) {
                // May fail if unregister won - OK
            }
        });

        // Thread B: unregister
        var unregisterFuture = executor.submit(() -> {
            try {
                Thread.sleep(1);
                coordinator.unregister(component.name());
            } catch (Exception e) {
                // May fail if started - OK
            }
        });

        registerFuture.get(1, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
        unregisterFuture.get(1, TimeUnit.SECONDS);

        // Check for leaked RUNNING component
        if (component.getState() == LifecycleState.RUNNING && 
            coordinator.getState(component.name()) == null) {
            failures.incrementAndGet();
        }
    } finally {
        // Cleanup: remove component if still registered
        try {
            if (coordinator.getState(component.name()) != null) {
                coordinator.stopAndUnregister(component.name());
            }
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Ignore cleanup errors
        }
    }
}
```

